  "doctrine": [],
  "note": "Arabic and Maltese preserve an n absent from Hebrew, Syriac and Akkadian. The Geʿez comparison ḫanzir (Anderson–Moser SEM000766) needs confirmation in a Geʿez text; Dillmann gives ሐራውያ in the dietary law. SEDRA lexeme 1003 covers both the plural pigs and the feminine sow. The personal name Hezir has the same consonants but a different first vowel, and neither list explains it."
